 "selection": "name -> index -> family -> bootloader. unknown name: profile by character trigram against the 41 measured corpora, take the FAMILY of the nearest match.",
 "law": "QUANTILE IS PER-CORPUS, NOT PER-FAMILY. measure H(depth) on the actual source and read it off: <0.7 -> 0.50, <1.0 -> 0.90, else 0.99. the family value is a FALLBACK for when no source is available. COBOL 0.582 and FORTRAN 1.279 share the \"fixed\" family and need different margins. and always round UP on an unseen dispatch key: falling back to the shallowest plane is the unsafe direction and cost 8.6 points of under-provisioning in Ada.",
